---
/**
 * The Docusaurus site shipped its own accordion (a React component plus a CSS
 * module) because MDX had no other way to collapse a block. Starlight has no
 * equivalent either, so it survives the migration as a pair of Astro
 * components — no client JS at all now, since `<details>` was always doing the
 * work and only the styling needed React's className plumbing.
 *
 * Colours come from the Starlight theme variables that @rxova/brand maps onto
 * the rxova tokens, so the accordion follows light/dark without a second set of
 * hardcoded values the way the CSS module did.
 */
---

<div class="doc-accordion">
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  .doc-accordion {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
</style>
